    "description": "Apply several commands atomically as one undo step: if any fails nothing is applied and the error path says which (commands/N/...). Prefer it for multi-step edits. Batches cannot nest. Each item is a tool's arguments plus its "type" (the command type of that tool, e.g. "room.setFloor" for room_set_floor). At most 50 commands per batch. Field meanings are those of the tool with the same name (not repeated in the schema).",
    "inputSchema": {
